:: Two-partition USB (legacy workflow: FAT32 WinPE boot + NTFS IMAGES data partition)
:: Drive letter is fixed at whatever letter the IMAGES partition gets (I: below is an example).
-WimFile "I:\images\Win11_Enterprise.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "I:\configs\unattend.xml" -DataDiskNumber 1 -EnableBitLocker -BitLockerPin "ReplaceWithYourPin42" -Force -Silent

:: Single-ISO workflow (build_iso.ps1 output — one file, Rufus to USB)
:: {DRIVE} is substituted at boot time with the actual drive letter WinPE assigns the USB.
:: build_iso.ps1 writes this file automatically; edit as needed before building.
-WimFile "{DRIVE}\images\Win11_Pro_Custom.wim" -TargetDisk 0 -UnattendFile "{DRIVE}\configs\unattend.xml" -Force -Silent

:: Interactive/TUI variant: pre-locates the WIM dir but prompts the operator
:: for edition selection, target disk, and confirmations. Good for lab/testing USBs.
-ImagePath "{DRIVE}\images"
